=TITLE CHANGES 

=head1 Upcoming

=item last entries, archive, feed and search markup now ask one predicate instead of four copies of a test that answered a different question
=item a page that carries a date no longer shows up in the feed as an entry

=head1 0.10.15

=item a mounted source may be given a section of the site with C<prefix>, and a source used as a version may not carry one: the address is built by one rule or the other

=item the build stops when a source declared as required gives the walk no files, and says so when an optional one does the same

=item a version of a mounted document names the source it is built from instead of a directory named by convention; a version whose optional source is missing is left out of the picker rather than offered as a dead link

=item a site may name the repositories its content comes from, and the build fetches them itself: the checkouts live beside the build, the content directory is left to the author, and a source declared as not required is skipped with a word instead of stopping the build

=head1 0.10.14

=item the check that stopped the build when a source declared a date the parse came back without is withdrawn: it asked the record before the plugins had made the page, so a paragraph carrying C<:pubdate> - a published note by design - stopped a site that builds

=head1 0.10.13

=item move to the 0.0.87 toolchain

=item a version of a mounted document declares its own answer: the permanent twin of the current version and a version not released yet stay out of both, a superseded version stays out of the search on the site

=item the search on the site skips a page that asks to stay out of it

=item a page may ask to stay out of a search engine with C<:noindex> and out of the search on the site with C<:nosearch>; the answer travels with the record, and the sitemap reads it from there

=item the build stops when a source declares an address or a date and the parse comes back without it: such a page used to disappear from the site without a word

=item the build reports what the linter finds in the sources on every run; C<--no-lint> skips the report, C<--lint-strict> stops the build on a problem

=item a site may declare several versions of a mounted document in C<spec-versions.json>: every entry names the address prefix and the branch or tag it is built from, and the file names the current one. Versions are read in the order they are written, oldest first

=item the current version answers at the address it has always answered at and once more at its own permanent address; the second copy points its canonical link at the first and asks to stay out of the index

=item a version that is not released yet is served with C<noindex> and left out of the sitemap; a superseded version keeps its own address in both

=item the list of versions is handed to the site as data, so the picker and the line of state are drawn by the site

=item the build stops when a declared version has no directory to read, and when a version that has one produces no page: both used to pass quietly and leave the picker pointing at an address that answers with nothing

=item a table is placed in the text column again: the previous release held it against the edge of the article, which on a wide window left it hundreds of pixels away from the paragraph above it. A table as wide as the column keeps the edge of the text, a narrower one is centred in the column

=item the caption of a narrow table reads as a sentence again: it used to be squeezed to the width of the table and fell into a column of single words, taller than the table it described. The caption is now drawn under the table and centred on it, and the space it needs is reserved exactly; the grid, its columns and the markup are untouched. On a screen too narrow for one line the caption moves above the table and wraps to the column

=head1 0.10.12

=item describe the page for a search engine with structured data: an entry with a date is an article and carries its headline and date, anything else is a page

=item declare the page language on the root element, taken from the site's C<:language> attribute and falling back to English

=item add a canonical address and the Open Graph title, description and address, so a shared link carries the page instead of a bare URL

=item build the address of a shared image from the site address: it was built from the page path, which gave a path where an address was needed

=item collapse the line break a title or description carries from the source, so it is not shown inside a meta tag

=head1 0.10.11

=item read the site address from C<SITE_URL> when no C<-s> is given: the flag carried a default that shadowed the variable, so setting it had no effect

=item find the index as C<index.podlite>, falling back to C<index.pod6>: a site no longer has to name it with the older extension, and one written with it keeps building unchanged

=item report the names that were looked for when neither index is present

=item the bundled examples are written with the C<.podlite> extension

=item the list of records draws one link per entry: a link held another link, which the browser cannot parse, so react rebuilt the whole page and the layout changed after loading

=item the cookie notice decides whether to appear after it is mounted, so the served page and the first render agree

=item the embedded editor is loaded in the browser only: it draws nothing without a window, and a page that serves it empty disagrees with the first render

=item keep the focus where it was when a page carries an embedded editor: the editor no longer takes it on mount, so the page stops jumping to it

=item find the page template even when the pubdate preset is on: a template carries no publication date and used to be dropped before the lookup

=item let a site template draw the page body: the component that renders a page is exported from the shared components, and the default template reaches it by the same path

=head1 0.10.10

=item the embedded editor renders again: the bundle carries one copy of the CodeMirror state and view packages instead of three

=item images carry the alt text declared in the document, and an empty alt when none is declared

=item move to the v0.0.84 toolchain, which reports a table whose rows disagree on the number of cells

=head1 0.10.9

=item move to the v0.0.83 toolchain, where an image with an unreadable orientation no longer stops the build

=head1 0.10.8

=item the feed states the language the site declares in C<:language>, falling back to english

=item move to the v0.0.82 toolchain

=head1 0.10.7

=item bump the C<@podlite> toolchain to the v0.0.81 release, where page records are written one per line with an index of their places

=item read one page record at a time instead of the whole list: the site build stopped at a corpus of 648 MB, where turning the list into a single string went past what the engine allows
=item drop two unused declarations in the page builder that filtered the whole list on every page and threw the result away

=head1 0.10.6

=item bump the C<@podlite> toolchain to the v0.0.80 release — a heading in a markdown file now reads with the same weight and colour as one in a podlite file, a markup code may be delimited by a run of angles, and a document holding the space-preserving code exports instead of stopping

=item pass the index file to the state-version plugin, so styles, favicon and images count towards the published state version and a change in them is noticed

=head1 0.10.5

=item bump the C<@podlite> toolchain to the v0.0.78 release — a heading anchor is shaped by the output rules, a link inside the document finds its heading, and a table row splits on two spaces

=item describe a page by its first sentence when it has no description of its own, instead of repeating the title

=item create the output directories before publishing, so a published image can build an external site

=head1 0.10.4

=item bump the C<@podlite> toolchain to the v0.0.77 release — a link keeps its target when the display text is formatted
=item name the page and the closest publish url when a slug resolves to nothing, instead of failing on an undefined record
=item let next handle image imports — the extra asset rule wrote a js module under the image url, so pages linked a file that was not an image
=item install dependencies after attaching an external site, so its workspace resolves during the build
=item add C<detach_path> to restore the workspace list and the config alias block that an external-site build rewrites
=item clear the leftover workspace entry that made every yarn command fail in a published image

=head1 0.10.3

=item upgrade to next 14 and react 18 — static export via C<output: 'export'>, swc minifier
=item drop next-optimized-images and next-compose-plugins; assets served via built-in webpack rules
=item import C<@podlite/to-jsx> and C<@podlite/editor-react> css in C<_app> (packages no longer auto-load it)
=item bump C<@podlite/*> toolchain (to-jsx 0.0.59, editor-react 0.0.61, publisher 0.0.35, schema 0.0.54, markdown 0.0.47, podlite 0.0.67)

=item render external links as plain anchors so archived urls with a second scheme in the path no longer fail the router during export

=item render external images (absolute, protocol-relative, and C<data:> urls) with a plain C<< <img> >> instead of looking them up in the prebuilt image map

=item degrade a missing local image to a small inline placeholder with a build warning instead of injecting a heading into the page

=head1 0.10.2

=item include C<podlite-web> version in C<control.json> C<stateVersion> via C<@podlite/publisher>'s C<appVersion> param; result format C<<crc>+v<publisher>+app<web>>

=item add C<themes/product.css>, C<themes/docs.css>, C<themes/minimal.css> companions to C<themes/portrait-avatar.css>; consumed by C<:theme<X>> attribute support в C<@podlite/publisher> site-data-plugin

=head1 0.10.1

=item extract header-img portrait styling to C<@Styles/themes/portrait-avatar.css>; default is neutral. Sites relying on the previous default add C<@import "@Styles/themes/portrait-avatar.css"> to their C<page.styles.css>

=head1 0.9.18

=item bump podlite 

=head1 0.9.17

=item bump podlite monorepo deps to 0.0.61

=head1 0.9.16

=item bump podlite monorepo deps to 0.0.60 — pulls in C<header> MIME parameter for CSV/TSV C<=data> blocks (C<@podlite/schema 0.0.40>) and recursive C<:folded> head section grouping with CSS margin fix (C<@podlite/to-jsx 0.0.44>)

=head1 0.9.15

=item fix image_block stretching to full screen width — small images now stay at natural size, large images capped at 38rem
=item add C<:enableFolding> attribute support for C<=PodLite> embedded editor (default C<false>)

